\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {One recorded failure, traced to its source.} (a)~The Eye's mass reports against the true masses; badges 1 and 2 mark the two items that are far off. (b)~The plan built on those reports stacks the notebook above the lighter pencil case, which breaks the heavy-at-the-bottom rule; the loop's attribution rule charges the failure to the Eye. (c)~Why it broke and two fixes: Arm challenges (5{} in this run) or a weighing probe. The strip below shows the three outcomes (scores 0.85{}, 0.99{} and 1.00{}). This is a symbolic fixture episode (seed 24{}, Eye mass noise $\sigma =0.45{}$, scripted Brain): a mechanism illustration, not a result.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{1}{2}{\textbf {One recorded failure, traced to its source.} (a)~The Eye's mass reports against the true masses; badges 1 and 2 mark the two items that are far off. (b)~The plan built on those reports stacks the notebook above the lighter pencil case, which breaks the heavy-at-the-bottom rule; the loop's attribution rule charges the failure to the Eye. (c)~Why it broke and two fixes: Arm challenges (\mechNChal {} in this run) or a weighing probe. The strip below shows the three outcomes (scores \mechNoFixScore {}, \mechChalScore {} and \mechProbeScore {}). This is a symbolic fixture episode (seed \mechSeed {}, Eye mass noise $\sigma =\mechSigma {}$, scripted Brain): a mechanism illustration, not a result}{figure.caption.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:mechanism@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][2][]2}{}{}{}}
